  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABC34tGg",
      "title": "validation: update standard proof params for Upgrade 20 game types",
      "author": "Wazabie",
      "number": 1331,
      "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nUpdates `standard-config-params-mainnet.toml` and `standard-config-params-sepolia.toml` so the standard proof parameters reflect [Upgrade 20](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/releases/tag/op-contracts%2Fv8.0.0-rc.3) (`op-contracts/v8.0.0`), which moves standard chains from Output Root to Super Root dispute games:\r\n\r\n- `respected_game_type`: `0` (`CANNON`) → `9` (`SUPER_CANNON_KONA`). Permissioned chains use `5` (`SUPER_PERMISSIONED`).\r\n- `[proofs.permissioned].game_type`: `1` (`PERMISSIONED_CANNON`) → `5` (`SUPER_PERMISSIONED`). The depth/clock parameters are dropped from this section: `SuperPermissionedDisputeGame` v1.1.0 is not a bisection game (no `maxGameDepth()` / `splitDepth()` / `maxClockDuration()` / `clockExtension()` getters) and resolves immediately as `DEFENDER_WINS`, subject to the air-gap.\r\n- New `[proofs.permissionless]` section for `SUPER_CANNON_KONA` (`9`) carrying the existing standard FDG parameters (`max_game_depth = 73`, `split_depth = 30`, `max_clock_duration = 302400`, `clock_extension = 10800`, matching op-deployer's standard defaults). The `ProofsParams` struct in `validation/params.go` already has a `permissionless` field, so no Go changes are needed.\r\n\r\nBoth `respected_game_type` and the permissioned `game_type` had been stale since Upgrade 19 (chains were already on `CANNON_KONA` 8, not `CANNON` 0). Codegen already classifies 5 as permissioned and 9 as permissionless since #1290.\r\n\r\n`ops/internal/report/testdata/expected-comment.md` is updated to match: the fixture is an `op-contracts/v1.6.0` deployment on game type 1, which no longer matches the standard, so the \"Permissioned Proofs\" rows now render as warnings.\r\n\r\nThese files are the governance-approved source of truth for the [Standard Rollup Charter](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/OPerating-manual/blob/main/Standard%20Rollup%20Charter.md) configuration check; the charter update re-pinning to this branch is ethereum-optimism/OPerating-manual#71.\r\n\r\n## Follow-ups (out of scope for this TOML change)\r\n\r\n- `ops/internal/report/l1.go` (`ScanFDG`) hardcodes game type `1` and reads bisection getters from the permissioned game, and `comment.md.tmpl` only renders the permissioned section. Both need updating before the staging report can validate a v8 deployment.\r\n- `standard-config-roles-*.toml` still lists `protocolVersionsOwner` although `ProtocolVersions` is removed in v8. Left unchanged here because `ops/internal/deployer/state.go` still writes it into op-deployer intents for older intent versions.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-09T17:45:20Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-25T21:32:24Z",
      "additions": 118,
      "deletions": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABES2jdw",
      "title": "fix(ops): surface forbidden L1 RPC responses",
      "author": "arunimshukla",
      "number": 1343,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- stop L1 RPC URL discovery when an endpoint returns HTTP 403\r\n- replace the misleading chain ID mismatch warning with a validation failure warning\r\n- add regression coverage for forbidden responses and legitimate chain ID fallback\r\n\r\n## Rationale\r\n\r\nA 403 response does not contain a chain ID. The existing code labels every validation error as a chain ID mismatch and continues to another URL, which can mask an authentication or access-control failure.\r\n\r\nThe new behaviour returns the wrapped HTTP error immediately while preserving fallback for an actual chain ID mismatch.\r\n\r\nCloses #1016.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `go test ./internal/config -count=1`\r\n- `go test -race ./internal/config -run 'TestFindValidL1URL' -count=1`\r\n- `go vet ./internal/config`\r\n- `git diff --check`",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-20T08:45:41Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 92,
      "deletions": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABFIi9_Q",
      "title": "chore: automated codegen update 2026-09-25",
      "author": "opgitgovernance",
      "number": 1349,
      "body": "This is an automated PR created by the daily-codegen circleci job.\n\nPlease review and merge if the changes look correct.\n\nNote that only these files should have been modified:\n\n- [addresses.json](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/blob/main/superchain/extra/addresses/addresses.json)\n- [chainList.json](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/blob/main/chainList.json)\n- [chainList.toml](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry/blob/main/chainList.toml)\n\nFor more details see the [runbook](https://www.notion.so/oplabs/superchain-registry-daily-codegen-294f153ee162803788cdee48ec542ca4?v=d784200583d9415587c4dcd2b0c64b2f).",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
